```json
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "I will implement this as a Go library, given Hyperledger Fabric's primary language and existing tooling.",
    "The library will provide functions that take existing configuration protobuf structures (e.g., *common.Config, *common.ConfigUpdate) and return modified versions, maintaining consistency with Fabric's internal patterns.",
    "For capabilities (U5), I will implement toggle functions (e.g., EnableV20ApplicationCapabilities()) rather than allowing arbitrary capability strings to ensure safety and alignment with Fabric's supported versions.",
    "All functions will be designed to be composable, allowing users to chain multiple configuration updates before computing the final ConfigUpdate transaction.",
    "Examples will be written as Go test functions within the test package, demonstrating practical usage for each category defined in U8."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "I have full access to the Hyperledger Fabric codebase and its Go modules for reference and dependency.",
    "The existing example test mentioned in U1, U2, U3, U5, U7, and U8 is a single Go test file that I will split and update as part of U8.",
    "I am familiar with Hyperledger Fabric's configuration structures and protobuf definitions.",
    "The development environment includes Go tooling and necessary Hyperledger Fabric dependencies.",
    "No external API or non-functional requirements (e.g., performance benchmarks) are required beyond the specified user stories.",
    "The library will be self-contained within a single Go package for simplicity, though internal organization will follow logical grouping."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Project Setup and API Design",
      "activity_description": "Initialize Go module, define package structure, and draft the public API signatures for all required functions. This includes reviewing Fabric's existing configuration helpers for patterns.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Orderer Endpoint Management (U1 & U2)",
      "activity_description": "Develop and unit test functions to add (U1) and remove (U2) orderer endpoints within an orderer organization's config group, including handling protobuf structures and validation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement Policy Retrieval (U3)",
      "activity_name": "Implement Policy Retrieval (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Create function to extract existing policies for any organization type (application, orderer, consortium) from a config transaction, returning a structured map or custom type.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Capability Retrieval (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Develop functions to retrieve orderer, application, and channel capabilities from a config transaction, returning the appropriate config.Capabilities protobuf type.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement Capability Modification (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Implement toggle functions (e.g., EnableV20ApplicationCapabilities) to add or remove specific supported capabilities for application, orderer, and channel sections. Includes design decisions for handling unsupported capabilities.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement Application Configuration Retrieval (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Develop function to parse and return the application configuration (config.Application) from a config transaction, simplifying access without manual protobuf traversal.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement ACL Modification (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Create functions to add or remove ACLs within an application group's configuration, ensuring compatibility with further configuration updates.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Example Refactoring and Writing (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Split the existing example test into separate, focused example functions as per U8 categories: orderer config, application config, organization management, MSP modifications, and capabilities. Update examples for U1-U7.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Integration Testing and Validation",
      "activity_description": "Write integration tests to verify end-to-end workflows, ensure composability of functions, and validate that generated ConfigUpdate transactions are correctly structured for signature workflows.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and Packaging",
      "activity_description": "Write GoDoc comments for all public functions, create a README with usage instructions, and prepare the library for release (e.g., tagging, module metadata).",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 16.0
  }
}
```

